course: dictionary
lesson: 6944
title: Adverbs that tell how
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Painlessly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. Look at its parts: painless is pain with -less, which means without, and -ly turns it into an adverb. So painlessly means in a way that causes no pain.
explain: «When an animal is very ill and cannot get better, a vet can end its suffering painlessly; this is called putting it to sleep.» The clue is suffering, which means pain or distress. Try your meaning in the sentence: a vet can end its suffering without causing pain. It still makes sense, so painlessly means without causing pain.
explain: Painlessly has a second meaning, about ease. «The test went painlessly» means it went smoothly, with no trouble or difficulty. «A tooth was taken out painlessly» shows the health meaning. Always check: does the sentence still make sense with your meaning swapped in?
fact: Painlessly means without causing pain.
fact: Painlessly can also mean easily, without trouble or difficulty.
fact: Painless is the adjective, and painlessly is the adverb that tells how something is done.
fact: «Painlessly» is often used about health, such as a tooth being taken out.
fact: The opposite of painlessly is painfully, which means causing pain or with great difficulty.
exercise: «The tooth was taken out painlessly.» What does painlessly mean here? | *Without causing pain | Bravely, with a shout | Very quickly, with a loud noise | Slowly and painfully
exercise: «The test went painlessly.» What does painlessly suggest? | Badly, with many mistakes | Loudly, with a lot of noise | *Easily, with no trouble | Late in the day
exercise: Which word tells you how something is done? | painful | *painlessly | pain | painless
test: «A vet can end an animal's suffering painlessly.» Which word has the opposite meaning? | Quietly | Easily | Happily | *Painfully
test: Ella says painlessly means with a sore head. What does it really mean? | With a big smile | *Without causing pain | Happily and loudly | Very sore and swollen
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The bandage came off painlessly»? | *Without any hurt, so it did not sting | Tightly, pulled hard round the arm | Angrily, as if cross | Very loudly and with a bang
